---
---

<section id="developer-suite" class="py-20 border-t border-zinc-200/80 bg-white dark:border-zinc-800/80 dark:bg-zinc-950">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl px-4 sm:px-6 space-y-24">
    
    <!-- Item 1: Developer Workspace -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">Developer Workspace</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">
          Hibernate forgotten projects, keep your source code intact
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          When you finish a client project or experiment with a new framework, its build artifacts (like <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">node_modules</code>, <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">target</code>, or <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">.venv</code>) stay on your SSD forever.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Beberes reads local Git commit timestamps to calculate project inactivity. With one click on <strong>Hibernate</strong>, only disposable dependencies are cleared. Your git history, source files, and environment configs remain untouched.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2.5 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Detects npm, pnpm, cargo, pip/poetry, go, gradle, and flutter caches
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Configurable inactivity threshold (30, 60, or 90 days)
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Reclaim 10 GB to 40 GB on average developer workstations
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-2 shadow-lg dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900">
          <img
            src="/screenshots/developer-workspace.png"
            alt="Developer Workspace Inactive Projects Screenshot"
            class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 w-full object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Item 2: Zombie Port Killer -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7 order-2 lg:order-1">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-2 shadow-lg dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900">
          <img
            src="/screenshots/zombie-ports.png"
            alt="Zombie Ports Killer Screenshot"
            class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 w-full object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-5 order-1 lg:order-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">Process Management</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">
          Kill ghost ports without terminal gymnastics
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Nothing interrupts a coding flow like <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-rose-500">EADDRINUSE: port 3000</code>. Usually, you have to run <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">lsof -i :3000</code>, find the PID, and type <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">kill -9 &lt;PID&gt;</code>.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Beberes lists all active listening TCP/UDP ports with their exact process names, memory footprints, and command line origins. Kill orphaned node, python, or docker servers in a single click with built-in PID safety guards.
        </p>
        <div class="mt-6 rounded-lg bg-zinc-100/80 p-3 text-xs text-zinc-700 dark:bg-zinc-900 dark:text-zinc-300 border border-zinc-200 dark:border-zinc-800 font-mono">
          $ beberes kill-port 3000 <span class="text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400"># Or use the GUI with 1-click</span>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Item 3: Deep App Uninstaller -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-10 items-center">
      <div class="lg:col-span-5">
        <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">App Hygiene</span>
        <h3 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-bold tracking-tight text-zinc-900 sm:text-3xl dark:text-white">
          Uninstall applications and hunt down their hidden remnants
        </h3>
        <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Dragging an app to the macOS Trash leaves behind gigabytes of cached data, container sandboxes, plist preferences, and launch agents.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Beberes matches app bundle identifiers across <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">~/Library</code> and <code class="text-xs bg-zinc-100 dark:bg-zinc-800 px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono">/Library</code> to show you exactly what will be deleted before anything is moved.
        </p>
        <ul class="mt-6 space-y-2.5 text-sm text-zinc-600 dark:text-zinc-300">
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Orphan leftover detection for already-deleted apps
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Protected system app whitelist (Finder, Dock, Safari cannot be removed)
          </li>
          <li class="flex items-center gap-2">
            <span class="h-1.5 w-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-500"></span>
            Detailed file preview with Quick Look support (Spacebar)
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <div class="rounded-xl border border-zinc-200 bg-zinc-50 p-2 shadow-lg dark:border-zinc-800 dark:bg-zinc-900">
          <img
            src="/screenshots/app-uninstaller.png"
            alt="App Uninstaller and Leftovers Hunter Screenshot"
            class="rounded-lg border border-zinc-200/80 dark:border-zinc-800/80 w-full object-cover"
            loading="lazy"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>
